+
+# Availability query for rental equipment
+
+## Request
+
+The desk needs to see at a glance what can still be rented. Add `availability(query)` to the rental
+service, where `query` is `{ start, end, kind }` and `kind` is optional. It returns the ids of the
+equipment of that kind, or of any kind when none is given, that is free for the whole period, sorted.
+
+## School rules (requirements)
+
+- R2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+- R3. A booking covers whole days: start and end are at midnight UTC, and the end is the start of the day
+  after the last rented day.
+- R4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1. `availability` is a method of the service returned by `createRentalService`. It takes
+  `{ start, end, kind? }` and returns a sorted array of item ids. (R2, R3)
+- AC2. An item is free when it has no booking overlapping `[start, end)`. Periods that only touch are
+  free. (R4)
+- AC3. Without `kind`, the result lists the free items of every kind. With `kind`, it lists only the free
+  items of that kind. (R4)
+- AC4. The result is sorted in ascending code-unit order, so it is the same on every call. (determinism)
+- AC5. `availability` throws for a `start` or `end` that is not a valid ISO-8601 UTC timestamp at midnight,
+  or an `end` that is not after the `start`. (R2, R3)
+- AC6. `availability` throws for a `kind` other than `'board'` or `'sail'`.
+- AC7. An item with no bookings is free. An empty result is an empty array, not an error.
+- AC8. Each service instance answers from its own equipment and bookings. (memory-only)
+
+## Test plan
+
+Test first (red, then green). Each acceptance criterion has at least one happy-path test and one
+error-path test. Tests are deterministic: no wall-clock time, no randomness, no external services.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Cancellations and refunds.
+- Persistence across restarts.
+- Availability for partial days.
+
+## Build record
+
+- Tests first: 13 tests in `tests/rental.test.ts` under `availability`, red before the method existed
+  (`service.availability is not a function`).
+- Implementation: `src/index.ts` adds `availability(query)` and the `AvailabilityQuery` type. The period
+  parsing moved to `parsePeriod`, and the overlap check to `clashes`, so `book` and `availability` share
+  one rule.
+- Result: `npm test` passes, 36 of 36 (23 existing, 13 new). Type-checking with `tsc` was not run: no
+  TypeScript compiler is installed in this repository.
+- Choices made: ids are sorted with `Array.prototype.sort` (code-unit order); an invalid `kind` throws
+  rather than returning an empty list; the period is validated the same way as for `quote` and `book`.
